# Subsystem placement (post-rescue)

Structural rescue is complete. New features are allowed again under these constraints:

## Do

- Put new sim logic in the matching `world_*.cpp` (or add a new `world_*.cpp` if none fits)
- Put UI / input / render / net glue in the matching `game_*.cpp`
- Extend `World::Cmd` + `applyCmd` for new player intents
- When adding sim fields: update `Ent`/`Player`, `checksum()`, and save/load together

## Do not

- Dump large new systems into `game.cpp` or `world.cpp` (keep those as thin facades)
- Call UI/SFX from `applyCmd` / combat / production paths
- Change checksum semantics without updating lockstep tests

See `docs/architecture.md`.
